Feature: F8 target — the TEKO_TARGET boundary (compile-fail; R2 honest error, teko-target-crosslink-0.3.1.md §0)

  # An unrecognised TEKO_TARGET must be a COMPILE error naming the value AND listing the supported
  # set — never a silent mis-lower to some other object format (the pre-0.3.1 arm64/Mach-O fallback,
  # which is how a linux x86_64 host came to emit a Mach-O arm64 object).
  #
  # ALL THREE NAME THE SAME BAD TARGET, and that is deliberate. They are three PROPERTIES of ONE
  # message: `unsupported_target_error` (src/build/project.tks) concatenates the offending name with
  # a fixed supported-set list, and every unrecognised spelling reaches it through the same
  # `target_from_name` lookup miss — so a second spelling re-proves the identical path and buys
  # nothing but a build. They used to declare three different bad names (`bogus-arch`,
  # `x86_64-solaris`, `not-a-target`) and cost three builds; sharing one, they cost ONE, because a
  # standalone `Given source` build is now cached per (file, declared env) — `regr_src_key`. The
  # value kept is the one a scenario actually ASSERTS by literal.
  Scenario: an unsupported TEKO_TARGET is an honest compile error listing the supported set
    Given target = "x86_64-solaris"
    Given source = "cases/target_boundary.tks"
    When compilation fails
    Then diagnostic = "unsupported TEKO_TARGET"

  Scenario: the unsupported-target diagnostic names the offending value
    Given target = "x86_64-solaris"
    Given source = "cases/target_boundary.tks"
    When compilation fails
    Then diagnostic = "x86_64-solaris"

  Scenario: the unsupported-target diagnostic lists a canonical supported name
    Given target = "x86_64-solaris"
    Given source = "cases/target_boundary.tks"
    When compilation fails
    Then diagnostic = "supported targets: x86_64-linux"

# PARSER rejections — folded from the retired `parse_diagnostics` project (0.3.1 consolidation).
# A parse error stops the compiler BEFORE the checker runs (§0.7, LEI), so these CANNOT share the
# checker-stage project build above (that build reaches the checker only because its own manifest and
# lexing succeed). Each rides as its OWN standalone `Given source` compile-fail build (immune to this
# project's checker-failing `src/`), which preserved twenty-four diagnostics verbatim at the 0.3.1
# consolidation. Five of those (`c02`/`c13`/`c14`/`c15`/`c16`, the null-sugar `T?`/`??`/`?.` friendly-
# diagnostic fixtures) were removed with the null-sugar retirement (theory/null-sugar) — the diagnostic
# they asserted no longer exists, so the row asserted nothing real. Nineteen remain — the honest price
# of the parse/checker stage boundary under the ten-project cap (the owner blessed extra compile-fail
# builds).
